Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage
player.player_id: join key to connect a person to batting or bowling events  
player.player_name: display the player’s name in the final list  
batsman_scored.match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no: align every run entry with a delivery in ball_by_ball  
batsman_scored.runs_scored: numerical value to be summed for every batsman  
ball_by_ball.match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no: join keys to reach striker (batsman id) and bowler id for the same ball  
ball_by_ball.striker: the batsman who scored the runs in that delivery  
ball_by_ball.bowler: the bowler who delivered the ball (used for wicket counts)  
wicket_taken.match_id / over_id / ball_id / innings_no: join keys to find which ball produced a wicket  
wicket_taken.player_out: batsman dismissed (not directly needed for this task)  
wicket_taken.kind_out: dismissal type – filter out 'run out', 'hit wicket', 'retired hurt'  
match.match_id: links every ball to the corresponding match  
match.season_id: groups all matches into seasons for season‑wise aggregation  

Typical conditions we will need later
WHERE wicket_taken.kind_out NOT IN ('run out','hit wicket','retired hurt')  
GROUP BY match.season_id, ball_by_ball.striker (or bowler)  
ORDER BY total_runs DESC, player_id ASC (tie‑breaker)  
LIMIT 3 (pick top 3 per season)  

Exploratory SQL queries  
Each query is limited to 20 rows and shows a different angle that will be helpful when building the final solution.

```sql
-- 1. List all seasons that exist in the data set
SELECT DISTINCT "season_id"
FROM "match"
ORDER BY "season_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect team names and their IDs
SELECT DISTINCT "team_id", "name"
FROM "team"
ORDER BY "team_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Explore the different dismissal kinds recorded
SELECT DISTINCT "kind_out"
FROM "wicket_taken"
ORDER BY "kind_out"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Get a quick look at player IDs and names
SELECT DISTINCT "player_id", "player_name"
FROM "player"
ORDER BY "player_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Sample the runs table: match/over/ball with runs scored
SELECT *
FROM "batsman_scored"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Join a run record to its striker (batsman) to verify linkage
SELECT b."match_id", b."over_id", b."ball_id", bb."striker", bs."runs_scored"
FROM "batsman_scored"  AS bs
JOIN "ball_by_ball"    AS bb
  ON bs."match_id"  = bb."match_id"
 AND bs."over_id"   = bb."over_id"
 AND bs."ball_id"   = bb."ball_id"
 AND bs."innings_no"= bb."innings_no"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Sample a wicket event joined with its bowler and dismissal type
SELECT w."match_id", w."over_id", w."ball_id", bb."bowler", w."kind_out"
FROM "wicket_taken" AS w
JOIN "ball_by_ball" AS bb
  ON w."match_id"  = bb."match_id"
 AND w."over_id"   = bb."over_id"
 AND w."ball_id"   = bb."ball_id"
 AND w."innings_no"= bb."innings_no"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Preview total runs per batsman in a season (example aggregation)
SELECT m."season_id",
       bb."striker"          AS "batsman_id",
       SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "total_runs"
FROM "batsman_scored" AS bs
JOIN "ball_by_ball"   AS bb ON
     bs."match_id"   = bb."match_id"
 AND bs."over_id"    = bb."over_id"
 AND bs."ball_id"    = bb."ball_id"
 AND bs."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
JOIN "match"         AS m  ON m."match_id" = bs."match_id"
GROUP BY m."season_id", bb."striker"
ORDER BY m."season_id", "total_runs" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Preview total wickets per bowler in a season (with dismissal filter)
SELECT m."season_id",
       bb."bowler"      AS "bowler_id",
       COUNT(*)         AS "total_wkts"
FROM "wicket_taken" AS w
JOIN "ball_by_ball" AS bb ON
     w."match_id"   = bb."match_id"
 AND w."over_id"    = bb."over_id"
 AND w."ball_id"    = bb."ball_id"
 AND w."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
JOIN "match"        AS m  ON m."match_id" = w."match_id"
WHERE w."kind_out" NOT IN ('run out','hit wicket','retired hurt')
GROUP BY m."season_id", bb."bowler"
ORDER BY m."season_id", "total_wkts" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Prototype: Top 3 run‑scorers & wicket‑takers for season 1, side‑by‑side
WITH top_bats AS (
   SELECT m."season_id",
          bb."striker" AS "player_id",
          SUM(bs."runs_scored") AS "runs",
          ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY m."season_id"
                             ORDER BY SUM(bs."runs_scored") DESC, bb."striker") AS rn
   FROM "batsman_scored" AS bs
   JOIN "ball_by_ball"   AS bb ON
        bs."match_id"   = bb."match_id"
    AND bs."over_id"    = bb."over_id"
    AND bs."ball_id"    = bb."ball_id"
    AND bs."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
   JOIN "match"         AS m  ON m."match_id" = bs."match_id"
   GROUP BY m."season_id", bb."striker"
), top_bowl AS (
   SELECT m."season_id",
          bb."bowler" AS "player_id",
          COUNT(*)    AS "wkts",
          ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY m."season_id"
                             ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC, bb."bowler") AS rn
   FROM "wicket_taken" AS w
   JOIN "ball_by_ball" AS bb ON
        w."match_id"   = bb."match_id"
    AND w."over_id"    = bb."over_id"
    AND w."ball_id"    = bb."ball_id"
    AND w."innings_no" = bb."innings_no"
   JOIN "match"        AS m  ON m."match_id" = w."match_id"
   WHERE w."kind_out" NOT IN ('run out','hit wicket','retired hurt')
   GROUP BY m."season_id", bb."bowler"
)
SELECT b."season_id",
       b."player_id" AS "batsman_id", b."runs",
       w."player_id" AS "bowler_id", w."wkts"
FROM top_bats AS b
JOIN top_bowl AS w
  ON b."season_id" = w."season_id" AND b.rn = w.rn
WHERE b."season_id" = 1
ORDER BY b.rn
LIMIT 20;
```
